    "lawCode": "Amd §396-i, Gen Bus L (as proposed in S.145-B & A.266-A)",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1329\n\nSPONSOR: THOMAS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to providing\nnotice of potential scams when selling gift cards\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to a chapter of the laws\nof 2022, enacting S.145B/A.266A.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by requiring the Consumer\nProtection Division of the Department of State to create a model notice\nand make it accessible to sellers.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Executive expressed a belief that requiring the Consumer Protection\nDivision to create a model notice making the template accessible to\nsellers would make it easier for sellers to comply with the law.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to a chapter of the laws of 2022, enacting\nS.145B/A.266A\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the General Business Law, in\nrelation to providing notice of potential scams when selling gift cards,\nas proposed in legislative bills numbers S.145B and A.266A, takes\neffect.\n",
